You are working on Coffee 2048.

Before meaningful work, read:
- docs/automation/PROJECT_RULES.md
- docs/automation/DEV_QUEUE.md
- docs/automation/ROADMAP.md
- docs/automation/CURSOR_EXECUTION_PROFILE.md
- AGENTS.md

The currently ACTIVE item in DEV_QUEUE is the hard upper boundary of autonomous work.
Do not implement later milestones unless the user explicitly expands the scope.

Core autonomous-development behavior:

1. REUSE FIRST.
   - Search existing code, UI, data, and assets before creating equivalents.
   - Existing puzzle, lobby, meta, customer, drink images, and UI assets are valuable project assets.
   - Never replace an existing implementation only because creating a new one is easier.

2. During an approved implementation milestone, include the UI/UX required to make the feature actually playable.
   - loading / empty / disabled / feedback states may be added without asking.
   - mobile/touch UX is part of completion.
   - stay consistent with the existing calm/premium/cozy design.

3. STOP for product-changing decisions.
   - core gameplay loop change
   - save-breaking change
   - major architecture replacement
   - major content deletion
   - existing primary-screen direction removal
   - paid API/service requirement

4. Do not silently delete or regenerate assets.
   - classify existing assets as REUSE / POLISH / LEGACY / NEEDED.
   - LEGACY does not mean safe to delete.

5. Do not perform unrelated refactors.

6. Existing review workflow remains mandatory.
   - lint
   - typecheck
   - build
   - relevant tests
   - UI visual checks when applicable
   - completion report

7. During M0 specifically:
   - analyze only
   - do not implement fixes
   - do not redesign UI
   - do not delete assets
   - write docs/automation/M0_REENTRY_REPORT.md

8. No extra paid AI/API automation.
   - do not introduce OpenAI API keys or other paid model APIs for unattended automation.
   - local tools and the user's existing Cursor/ChatGPT/Codex access are preferred.

When a blocking product decision is discovered, stop and report using:

# DECISION REQUIRED
## Current task
## Problem
## Why approval is required
## Options
## Recommendation
## Impact
